quillify redistributes four files that are other projects' work. Everything
else it depends on is installed by its consumer and is not in the package.

assets/pdf.worker.js
  The worker of pdf.js: build/pdf.worker.mjs of pdfjs-dist 6.4.299,
  Copyright 2024 Mozilla Foundation, under the Apache License 2.0
  (licenses/pdf.js-LICENSE).
  Changed: a null guard added at two sites, a page's first unsplittable
  node no longer taken from an overflow leader or trailer, a page set made to
  clear its page areas' counts when it starts another pass, a field with no
  control or a default one given a text control, a field whose control has no
  HTML given a box for it so that its caption is laid out, a list bound to
  data the file does not hold left with the items its template lists, a span
  marked where a page's text embeds a page number or a page count that a
  layout script fills, an exception of the XFA layout thrown on after it is
  logged, and the last line, which named a source map, removed. The file's
  first line says the same.

assets/xfa-layer.js
  Lines 1270 to 1588 of web/pdf_viewer.css of pdfjs-dist 6.4.299, unchanged,
  under a header comment and as the text of a JavaScript module.
  Copyright 2014 Mozilla Foundation, under the Apache License 2.0
  (licenses/pdf.js-LICENSE).

assets/qpdf.worker.js
  dist/qpdf.js of @neslinesli93/qpdf-wasm 0.3.0, unchanged, under a first
  line that says so and above a message handler that is quillify's own. It is
  the script that loads assets/qpdf.wasm and runs it. That package declares
  the ISC license and ships no license text. The script names no author and
  no license. It is the JavaScript that Emscripten writes beside a binary it
  compiles, and Emscripten's own code is under the MIT license and the
  University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source License, whose texts are not in
  that package, and so not in licenses/.

assets/qpdf.wasm
  dist/qpdf.wasm of @neslinesli93/qpdf-wasm 0.3.0, unchanged. Its SHA-256 is
  abd933f4ccace4f732999381b21aec8b7e3726f18a5b167fafd57f88dd440876.
  That package declares the ISC license and ships no license text. The binary
  is a build of qpdf 12.2.0, Copyright (c) 2005-2021 Jay Berkenbilt and
  Copyright (c) 2022-2025 Jay Berkenbilt and Manfred Holger, under the Apache
  License 2.0, whose text is the one in licenses/pdf.js-LICENSE. zlib and
  libjpeg-turbo 2.1.1 are linked into it, and so is a C++ runtime.

  Not in that package, and so not in licenses/: the license texts of zlib, of
  libjpeg-turbo and of that runtime, and the notices qpdf carries in its
  NOTICE.md for code it embeds. In qpdf 12.4.0 those are for sphlib 3.0 and
  for a Rijndael implementation; the NOTICE.md of 12.2.0 was not read.
